'' '#cmdline' IS NOT IMPLEMENTED AND NOW SAYS SO. It was skipped in silence, which
'' is the worst of the three available answers: the corpus writes
'' '#cmdline "-d CMDLINESYMBOL"' and '#cmdline "-w error"', so skipping it leaves
'' the symbol undefined or the warnings not-errors, and the file compiles into
'' something the author did not ask for with nothing said anywhere.
''
'' IT IS NOT THE SAME SHAPE as '#inclib' and '#libpath', which is why it is reported
'' rather than implemented alongside them. Those name one thing the link needs.
'' '#cmdline' injects arbitrary OPTIONS from inside a source already being compiled
'' under the options it wants to change -- fbc's answer is '-restart', re-invoking
'' itself with the new command line. Anything less is a subset that works until
'' someone writes the option that needs the restart.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0310
'' EXPECT-OUT: '#cmdline' is not implemented in this build

#cmdline "-d CMDLINESYMBOL"
print "x"
